  "findings": [
    "Trilogy's second side head (#9, Three-claw head at 118 deg, spin -90) tessellates with 2 degenerate faces in its own part mesh at the export chord (builds of 512 steps and up, EXPORT_CHORD_MM 0.015); its mirror twin #6 and every other made part are clean, and the resolved ring mesh is watertight with 0 degenerate faces, so ring exports are unaffected. The starter test checks part meshes at the preview chord only (192 x 96), where #9 is clean. The fix belongs in the claw builder (P6).",
    "Opened from the menu, a sand-ready stock's source is named 'Signet NNN / drafted workshop master'; the desktop Design panel's Imported signet base picker matches presets by the plain stock name, so it shows that raw name instead of selecting the preset.",
    "CLAUDE.md (not in this worktree's sparse checkout) still describes the template gallery as nine starters and nine committed template graphs; the code now has 13 code starters, 13 bundled starter graphs and 20 factory stocks."
  ],
  "open_items": [
    "Officina (six lessons) is not built; the Workshop collection stays in its menu slot until it is, so the menu count stays at 55 (57 once Officina replaces Workshop).",
    "Workshop retirement (assets DESIGNS rows, previews, sources.json entries, workshop_collection.rs and its tools) waits for Officina.",
    "Part 2: Wishbone wave returns only with ShankKey::slide (C-S6); Trilogy and Toi et moi carry ovals until true pear plans (C-B2).",
    "Phone release steps not done by rule: no version bump or CHANGELOG entry (Logan's standing rule), and no rdsmoke AVD smoke test (no emulators in this lane). The retired phone menu item needs a CHANGELOG line at the next release.",
    "Nothing pushed, merged into master, tagged or published."
